Thanks, Fernando! Attached are the three scripts:
dataStructs.R provides the functions used to automate the walk-through in rglstuff.R;
rglstuff.R is a walk-through, trying to provide visualization of different data structures. Though it’s not very self-documenting, most of the examples show the code that is being depicted. I have some thoughts on how to improve this, and will likely be improving this in the future on the groups Github site <https://github.com/GRUMP> (project forthcoming).
notes.R is the remainder of the talk, walking through the R functions of *apply, dplyr, tidyr, etc.

Questions, comments, suggestions, and pull-requests are welcome!

-r2

